# Claude Code — project rules and skills are tracked, local session state is not.
#
# WHY: `.claude/` was ignored wholesale, and `EnterWorktree` therefore produced a worktree with
# ZERO project rule files against 10 in the main checkout. The whole feat/ux-overhaul branch —
# the largest UI task in this repo — ran without designsystem.md / ui-card-patterns.md /
# adaptive-navigation.md, i.e. without the very files CLAUDE.md points at for UI rules
# (found 2026-08-17). `.worktreeinclude` papered over it by copying; tracking fixes it.
#
# settings.json stays out deliberately: it is a per-machine permission grant, not a project rule.
#
# `.claude/skills/` stays out too, and NOT for tidiness: `ai-chat-feedback-fixer/
# processed-feedback.md` is a verbatim log of real end users' chat messages mined from
# Amplitude — other people's text, some of it personal. Publishing it would be a privacy
# incident, not a numbers leak. Open the skills directory only after that file is moved out or
# redacted, and re-scan the rest for the Amplitude project id and account addresses it also
# carries.
#
# `.claude/hooks/` also stays out: `guard-main-repo-edit.ps1` hardcodes this machine's checkout
# path twice (`c:\users\admin\…`) — the exact shape this policy strips out of CLAUDE.md, and one
# the scanner cannot catch there because it only reads *.md. Track it once the roots come from
# `git rev-parse` instead of a literal.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/

# graphify knowledge graph — local dev-tool output, not portfolio code
graphify-out/

